    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20148" root="سقى" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَقَّآءٌ</span></b> ; and the fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَقَّآءَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَقَّايَةٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاقٍ</span>,
in six places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّقَّآءُ</span> is also the appellation of
<i>A certain intelligent bird, that draws water for
itself.</i> (JK.) [It is applied in the present day,
by some, to <i>The pelican:</i> and by some, to <i>the
aquiline vulture; commonly called the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَخَم</span>.]

